sibling in the path

4. **up**: Reconstructs the parent node from the path and moves focus up

5. **toTree**: Reconstructs the full tree by walking back up to the root

6. **setValue/setLeft/setRight**: Create modified copies of the current node 
while preserving the path



The key insight is that the path stores enough information (parent value and 
sibling subtree) to reconstruct any ancestor node when navigating up or 
converting back to a tree.

