I'll analyze this problem and implement a solution.

The key insight is that we need to find the grouping that maximizes the discount. A greedy approach (always forming the largest possible sets) doesn't always work, as shown in the example where grouping into two sets of 4 is cheaper than a set of 5 and a set of 3.

The approach:
1. Count copies of each book
2. Greedily form sets (largest possible distinct sets first)
3. Apply a correction: replace any combination of a set of 5 + set of 3 with two sets of 4, since that's cheaper ($51.20 vs $51.60)

Here's my implementation:

book-store.js
```js
//
// This is only a SKELETON file for the 'BookStore' exercise. It's been provided as a
// convenience to get you started writing code faster.
//

const BOOK_PRICE = 800;
const DISCOUNTS = {
  1: 0,      // 0% discount
  2: 0.05,   // 5% discount
  3: 0.10,   // 10% discount
  4: 0.20,   // 20% discount
  5: 0.25,   // 25% discount
};

export const cost = (books) => {
  // Count the number of copies of each book
  const counts = new Array(5).fill(0);
  for (const book of books) {
    counts[book - 1]++;
  }

  // Greedily form sets: each set contains one copy of each of the most available books
  const sets = [];
  while (counts.some(c => c > 0)) {
    // Sort counts descending, take only those > 0
    const sorted = counts
      .filter(c => c > 0)
      .sort((a, b) => b - a);
    // Form a set from the top books
    const setSize = sorted.length;
    sets.push(setSize);
    // Decrement the counts for the books in this set
    for (let i = 0; i < setSize; i++) {
      counts[i]--;
    }
  }

  // Correction: replace any (5, 3) pair with (4, 4) as it's cheaper
  // Count sets of size 5 and 3
  let numSetsOf5 = 0;
  let numSetsOf3 = 0;
  const correctedSets = [];
  for (const setSize of sets) {
    if (setSize === 5) {
      numSetsOf5++;
    } else if (setSize === 3) {
      numSetsOf3++;
    }
  }
  
  // Each (5,3) pair becomes (4,4)
  const numCorrections = Math.min(numSetsOf5, numSetsOf3);
  for (let i = 0; i < numCorrections; i++) {
    correctedSets.push(4);
    correctedSets.push(4);
  }
  
  // Add remaining sets (excluding those that were part of (5,3) pairs)
  let used5 = 0;
  let used3 = 0;
  for (const setSize of sets) {
    if (setSize === 5 && used5 < numCorrections) {
      used5++;
      continue;
    }
    if (setSize === 3 && used3 < numCorrections) {
      used3++;
      continue;
    }
    correctedSets.push(setSize);
  }

  // Calculate total cost
  let totalCost = 0;
  for (const setSize of correctedSets) {
    const discount = DISCOUNTS[setSize];
    totalCost += setSize * BOOK_PRICE * (1 - discount);
