4. Returning the appropriate game state

Let me analyze the logic:
- X starts, so counts must be: `count(X) == count(O)` or `count(X) == count(O) + 1`
- If X has won, then X must have made the last move, so `count(X) == count(O) + 1`
- If O has won, then O must have made the last move, so `count(X) == count(O)`
- Both players can't win simultaneously
- The game can't continue after someone wins

Here's my implementation:

StateOfTicTacToe.java
```java
class StateOfTicTacToe {
    public GameState determineState(String[] board) {
        int xCount = 0;
        int oCount = 0;
        
        for (String row : board) {
            for (char c : row.toCharArray()) {
                if (c == 'X') {
                    xCount++;
                } else if (c == 'O') {
                    oCount++;
                }
            }
        }
        
        // Check turn order validity
        if (oCount > xCount || xCount > oCount + 1) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid turn order");
        }
        
        boolean xWins = hasWon(board, 'X');
        boolean oWins = hasWon(board, 'O');
        
        // Check for invalid states where game continued after win
        if (xWins && oWins) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Both players cannot win");
        }
        
        if (xWins) {
            if (oCount == xCount) {
                // O moved after X won, invalid
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Game continued after X won");
            }
            return GameState.WIN;
        }
        
        if (oWins) {
            if (xCount == oCount) {
                // X moved after O won, invalid
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Game continued after O won");
            }
            return GameState.WIN;
        }
        
        // No winner yet
        if (xCount + oCount == 9) {
            // Board is full, it's a draw
            return GameState.DRAW;
        }
        
        // Game is ongoing
        return GameState.ONGOING;
    }
    
    private boolean hasWon(String[] board, char player) {
        // Check rows
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
            if (board[i].charAt(0) == player && 
                board[i].charAt(1) == player && 
                board[i].charAt(2) == player) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        
        // Check columns
        for (int j = 0; j < 3; j++) {
            if (board[0].charAt(j) == player && 
                board[1].charAt(j) == player && 
                board[2].charAt(j) == player) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        
        // Check diagonals
        if (board[0].charAt(0) == player && 
            board[1].charAt(1) == player && 
            board[2].charAt(2) == player) {
            return true;
        }
        
        if (board[0].charAt(2) == player && 
            board[1].charAt(1) == player && 
            board[2].charAt(0) == player) {
            return true;
        }
        
        return false;
    }
}
```

