Applied edit to beer_song.py
The test failure shows that decoding `0xffffffff` (the maximum 32-bit unsigned 
integer) fails because the code masks the value with `0x7FFFFFFF` during 
accumulation, which truncates the top bit. The fix is to accumulate in an 
unmasked `uint64` and then validate that the result fits within 32 bits before 
converting to `uint32`.



