The function signature needs to accept parameters. Based on the description, it should take the list of base values and the level number.

sum-of-multiples.js
```
//
// This is only a SKELETON file for the 'Sum Of Multiples' exercise. It's been provided as a
// convenience to get you started writing code faster.
//

export const sum = (items, level) => {
  const multiples = new Set();

  for (const item of items) {
    if (item === 0) {
      // Multiples of 0 are only 0, which we skip if level > 0
      // (0 is not less than any positive level, and adding 0 doesn't change sum)
      continue;
    }
    for (let multiple = item; multiple < level; multiple += item) {
      multiples.add(multiple);
    }
  }

  let total = 0;
  for (const multiple of multiples) {
    total += multiple;
  }

  return total;
};
```
