I'll implement the PhoneNumber class to clean up phone numbers according to the NANP rules.

Here's the implementation:

PhoneNumber.java
```java
class PhoneNumber {
    private final String number;

    PhoneNumber(String numberString) {
        // Check for letters
        for (char c : numberString.toCharArray()) {
            if (Character.isLetter(c)) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Letters not permitted in number");
            }
        }

        // Check for invalid punctuation
        for (char c : numberString.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '!' || c == '@') {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Punctuation not permitted");
            }
        }

        // Extract only digits
        StringBuilder digitsOnly = new StringBuilder();
        for (char c : numberString.toCharArray()) {
            if (Character.isDigit(c)) {
                digitsOnly.append(c);
            }
        }

        String digits = digitsOnly.toString();

        // Check number of digits
        if (digits.length() < 10) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Must not be fewer than 10 digits");
        }
        if (digits.length() > 11) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Must not be more than 11 digits");
        }

        // Handle country code
        if (digits.length() == 11) {
            if (digits.charAt(0) != '1') {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Country code must be 1");
            }
            digits = digits.substring(1);
        }

        // Now digits should be exactly 10
        // Check area code (first digit of 10-digit number)
        if (digits.charAt(0) == '0') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Area code must not start with 0");
        }
        if (digits.charAt(0) == '1') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Area code must not start with 1");
        }

        // Check exchange code (first digit of local 7-digit number)
        if (digits.charAt(3) == '0') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Exchange code must not start with 0");
        }
        if (digits.charAt(3) == '1') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Exchange code must not start with 1");
        }

        this.number = digits;
    }

    String getNumber() {
        return number;
    }
}
```
