I'll implement the Resistor Color Trio exercise. Let me analyze the requirements:

1. Take 3 colors as input
2. First two colors form a two-digit number
3. Third color indicates how many zeros to add
4. Output the value in ohms, using metric prefixes (kiloohms, megohms, gigohms) when appropriate

resistor-color-trio.js
```
//
// This is only a SKELETON file for the 'Resistor Color Trio' exercise. It's been provided as a
// convenience to get you started writing code faster.
//

export class ResistorColorTrio {
  constructor() {
    this.colorCodes = {
      black: 0,
      brown: 1,
      red: 2,
      orange: 3,
      yellow: 4,
      green: 5,
      blue: 6,
      violet: 7,
      grey: 8,
      white: 9
    };
  }

  label(colors) {
    const firstValue = this.colorCodes[colors[0]];
    const secondValue = this.colorCodes[colors[1]];
    const zeros = this.colorCodes[colors[2]];

    const currentValue = (firstValue * 10 + secondValue) * Math.pow(10, zeros);

    let unit = 'ohms';
    let value = currentValue;

    if (currentValue >= 1000000000) {
      unit = 'gigohms';
      value = currentValue / 1000000000;
    } else if (currentValue >= 1000000) {
      unit = 'megohms';
      value = currentValue / 1000000;
    } else if (currentValue >= 1000) {
      unit = 'kiloohms';
      value = currentValue / 1000;
    }

    return `${value} ${unit}`;
  }
}
```
