I'll implement the Series class to generate contiguous digit substrings of a specified length.

Series.java
```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.ArrayList;

class Series {
    private final String digits;

    Series(String string) {
        this.digits = string;
    }

    List<String> slices(int num) {
        if (num <= 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Slice size must be positive");
        }
        if (num > digits.length()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Slice size cannot be greater than string length");
        }

        List<String> slices = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i <= digits.length() - num; i++) {
            slices.add(digits.substring(i, i + num));
        }
        return slices;
    }
}
```
