Looking at the code, the `plants(const std::string&, const std::string&)` function uses a hardcoded list of children names, but the exercism tests may pass custom student names. The standard exercism test uses the two-argument version with a vector of student names to define the class ordering.

The correct signature for the single-child version should accept the list of students so the alphabetical ordering can be computed from the provided names.

