This looks reasonable to me. Let me verify it handles the key requirements:

1. ✅ Input cells with settable values
2. ✅ Compute cells computed from other cells  
3. ✅ Value propagation when inputs change
4. ✅ Callback registration that fires when values change in stable state

The implementation uses a dependency graph where each cell tracks its dependents. When a cell's value changes, it notifies all dependent cells, which will recompute and potentially notify their dependents in turn. Callbacks only fire when a cell's value actually changes.
